<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Marvellous. It is marvellous.\'92 Sarah gazed out in wonder over the city a crystal blue harbour, scintillating and twinkling, at the points and bays, the cramming of buildings all the way to the water\'92s edge. Her eyes followed the sweep of the harbour as it flowed east then swept left where it met its north arm and flowed out to the ocean which extended in placid, eternal blue until it merged with the forever of the sky.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Come sit.\'92 Eloise guided Sarah to the couch ensemble farther away from the windows. \'91Coffee?\'92 Sarah nodded and Eloise poured.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91There\'92s a meeting I want you to take, as your first task as head of the project. It\'92s a bit of house-cleaning, I\'92m afraid. A meeting I\'92ve been putting off, hoping it will go away, but it hasn\'92t.\'92 Eloise shrugged. \'91You have complete freedom to do as you wish. To be honest, I rather expect you\'92ll handle this one much better than I ever could.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Who\'92s it with?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise enjoyed the mystery as she sipped her coffee. \'91You\'92ll see.\'92\
