<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny sat on the bespoke monkey-leather couch in the expansive reception outside Eloise\'92s office and smugly declined coffee. He rested an ankle on a knee and admired his shoes. While his perfectly pink hands clasped and relaxed in his lap, he examined his smugly manicured fingernails and contemplated how much he would make Eloise Shakti beg to take him back.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You can go in now,\'92 said the receptionist, who Johnny was sure Eloise selected for her singular ability to repel the male gaze.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny stood and grimaced, determined to ignore the receptionist for the lack of sexual chemistry he felt for her. And so he was looking at nothing in particular when he wrenched the door open and stepped inside.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Ah, Mr Stoat,\'92 said the woman rising behind the desk, and was approaching him with rather too much sexual attraction for his comfort, and who was, in any case, not Eloise Shakti.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Thank you for coming,\'92 the woman said. \'91Let\'92s sit over here, shall we?\'92\
